# KB persistence (mandatory)

This repo is a **Second Brain**. Session knowledge lives in `docs/conversations/`, not only in chat.

## When answering (learning / factual prompts)

1. **Search `docs/` first** (structured notes + past sessions in `docs/conversations/`) before web search or model recall.
2. **One topic per message** — short replies; do not dump whole syllabus blocks in chat.
3. **Every turn with new content** → append/update **one** `##` section in the **current session file** under `docs/conversations/` (one `.md` per session). Do not only answer in chat.
4. **Plan at top of session file:** `# Plan sesji` with `## Nauka` and `## Quiz` — each topic gets a matching `Quiz: …` checkbox; one checkbox ≈ one future message.
5. **Do not ask permission** to save. Format: see `docs/conversations/README.md`.
6. **Structured KB** (`docs/sailing/`, …) — update **only when the user asks**, or run `npm run kb:promote -- <session.md> <target/path>` then `npm run sync`.
7. After editing structured `docs/` (not conversations), **run `npm run sync`** (`docker-compose up -d` if needed).
8. **Commit** when the turn produced file edits. **Never push** unless the user explicitly asks.

## Exemptions

- Pure app-development (`lib/`, `mcp_server/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, `context/changes/`).
- Trivial replies ("ok", "done", clarifying questions).

## If KB already has the answer

Read and cite existing notes or session history. Update structured notes only when asked.
